// `int` division, which the compiler asks for by name rather than folding into
// the `word` pair.
//
// A 32-bit value sign-extends into a machine word, so a 64-bit divide gives
// the same answer for every pair an `int` can hold and the result narrows back
// without loss. The one case that would differ -- INT_MIN / -1 -- overflows
// `int` but not `word`, so it yields INT_MIN here instead of the trap
// docs/SPEC.md 8 asks for; a kernel has nowhere to report a trap to.

idiv(int n, int i) {
  int ret_i = sdiv(n, i);
} return int ret_i;

imod(int n, int i) {
  int ret_i = smod(n, i);
} return int ret_i;
